>...
>Do the DEC/MIPS/RISC workstations use IEEE floating point or VAX floating
>point internal representations?

The MIPS-based DECstations use IEEE floating-point and little-endian byte
ordering.  This makes them completely data-format compatible with the
Intel x86 family of processors, which may be interesting if you're
attempting to share data with PCs.

