In article <10689@lcra.uucp>, mike@lcra.uucp (Mike O'Donnell) writes...
>Long ago and far away our MicroVAX II's outgrew their RD53 disk 
>drives.  Is it possible to use these drives for PCs or
>Macs?  Are there controllers available to support them?

RD53s are Micropolis 1325s or 1335s which are standard ST506-interface hard
disks (the difference between those two is in MTBF).  These can be used
directly on most PC controllers.  For a Macintosh, you'd need an adapter board
that tranlates from SCSI to ST506; Adaptec makes a couple boards with differing
features.

Chris


