   and others and no one complains about the crappy displays.  Why?  Is there a
   fix for this that we don't know about?

I think "crappy" is a definite overstatement -- in many ways I prefer
the DS3100 display, but they do have a lower refresh rate: 60 Hz, in fact --
the same as the rate at which neon lights flicker.  That means that if you
have neon lights on, you can get some serious interference between them and
the monitor that can potentially lead to headaches.  You might try using
incandescent lights (or no lights at all) as an experiment -- do your
headaches go away then?

